  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive).\n\nUSAGE:\nSense 1 takes を to mark what is revealed: {秘密|ひみつ}を{明|あ}かす, {正体|しょうたい}を{明|あ}かす.\nSense 2 is often used as a compound verb suffix: V{連用形|れんようけい} + {明|あ}かす (e.g., {語|かた}り{明|あ}かす, {飲|の}み{明|あ}かす). Also used as {夜|よる}を{明|あ}かす (to spend the whole night).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {秘密|ひみつ}を{明|あ}かす: to reveal a secret\n- {正体|しょうたい}を{明|あ}かす: to reveal one's identity\n- {夜|よる}を{明|あ}かす: to stay up all night\n- {語|かた}り{明|あ}かす: to talk all night long\n- {飲|の}み{明|あ}かす: to drink all night long\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {暴|あば}く: to expose, to uncover (forceful)\n- {打|う}ち{明|あ}ける: to confide, to open up about",
